      "message": "1:1 would mean that libcore/libart was a package, but it\u0027s not, because it doesn\u0027t contain an Android.bp file.\n\nI\u0027m not sure how to deal with libcore/JavaLibrary.bp.  Does that type of include concept exist in Bazel?  I know you can include starlark files that define macros, but can you include a file that defines modules?  If so, I\u0027d suggest following Bazel\u0027s semantics, whatever they are.\n\nIf not, then we should probably just forbid crossing subdirectory boundaries, and treat them as the same package.",
